            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "3f68de7c-d729-4b62-9bb1-36c6f518fea4",
               "text": "Equipe History Tracers — Simplicidade vs. Complexidade",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=3f68de7c-d729-4b62-9bb1-36c6f518fea4",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2025",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### O Papel\n\nAnteriormente, também dividimos uma folha de papel em dez partes. Mas imagine que fazemos uma divisão menor e cortamos a folha apenas ao meio. Então ficamos com duas metades da folha.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 200\" width=\"100%\"><rect x=\"30\" y=\"20\" width=\"280\" height=\"160\" fill=\"#ADD8E6\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"170\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"170\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></svg></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "A sheet of paper divided into two equal halves.",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "90042b52-222f-4e82-9212-13e52e885c59",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "90042b52-222f-4e82-9212-13e52e885c59",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "inlove",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "9b0e87f9-e372-49d4-979e-4ba9742f70e1",
               "text": "Texto Original",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=9b0e87f9-e372-49d4-979e-4ba9742f70e1",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            },
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "0836cb37-3574-4ca8-9efa-d3fd158b0805",
               "text": "Weisstein, Eric W.",
               "page": "https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Fraction.html",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Uma Nova Representação\n\nNas aulas anteriores e nesta, vimos que as coisas podem ser unificadas ou reunidas, e também observamos que podem ser divididas.\n\nPara apresentar as duas ideias juntas, vamos usar a ideia de fração. Em uma fração, escrevemos as partes em cima — o numerador — e o total embaixo — o denominador. Uma barra separa os dois.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<style>.frac{display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;text-align:center;margin:0 6px;white-space:nowrap;}.frac .n{display:block;padding:0 6px;border-bottom:2px solid #222222;white-space:nowrap;}.frac .d{display:block;padding:0 6px;white-space:nowrap;}.eq{text-align:center;font-size:26px;color:#222222;margin:8px 0;}</style><p class=\"eq\" style=\"font-size:26px;\"><span class=\"frac\"><span class=\"n\">numerador</span><span class=\"d\">denominador</span></span></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "A fraction with the numerator on top and the denominator below.",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "f7992453-d1ac-42db-b749-7156478e15e8",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "f7992453-d1ac-42db-b749-7156478e15e8",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "happy",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "9b0e87f9-e372-49d4-979e-4ba9742f70e1",
               "text": "Texto Original",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=9b0e87f9-e372-49d4-979e-4ba9742f70e1",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            },
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "7a9c733b-ca13-40f5-8849-19012540b028",
               "text": "Ernst, Dana.",
               "page": "https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Mathematical_Logic_and_Proof/An_Introduction_to_Proof_via_Inquiry-Based_Learning_(Ernst)/05%3A_New_Page/5.01%3A_New_Page",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            },
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "68227419-2430-4359-b902-f6cf87b8941d",
               "text": "Holmes, F. L.",
               "page": "https://books.google.com.br/books?hl=en&lr=&id=MLY-x9a393QC",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "1985",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Juntos\n\nVamos usar a nossa representação em fração para entender o que vemos nesta página. Comecemos com as duas metades do papel. Quando as duas partes estão unidas, podemos representá-las como 2 pedaços juntos no numerador, divididos pelo total de 2, o que é igual a 1. Como vimos, quando tudo está junto, é apenas 1.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<style>.frac{display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;text-align:center;margin:0 6px;white-space:nowrap;}.frac .n{display:block;padding:0 6px;border-bottom:2px solid #222222;white-space:nowrap;}.frac .d{display:block;padding:0 6px;white-space:nowrap;}.eq{text-align:center;font-size:26px;color:#222222;margin:8px 0;}</style><p class=\"eq\" style=\"font-size:26px;\"><span class=\"frac\"><span class=\"n\">2</span><span class=\"d\">2</span></span> = 1</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "Two over two equals one.",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "69d13f0f-1fec-4b9e-944e-a3cb944852f4",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "69d13f0f-1fec-4b9e-944e-a3cb944852f4",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "shocking",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "9b0e87f9-e372-49d4-979e-4ba9742f70e1",
               "text": "Texto Original",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=9b0e87f9-e372-49d4-979e-4ba9742f70e1",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            },
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "68227419-2430-4359-b902-f6cf87b8941d",
               "text": "Holmes, F. L.",
               "page": "https://books.google.com.br/books?hl=en&lr=&id=MLY-x9a393QC",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "1985",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Dividido\n\nQuando cortamos uma folha de papel ao meio, ficamos com duas partes, em vez da peça única que tínhamos antes.\n\nRepresentamos essa situação escrevendo um sobre dois (1/2). E voltamos à situação anterior somando as duas partes.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<style>.frac{display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;text-align:center;margin:0 6px;white-space:nowrap;}.frac .n{display:block;padding:0 6px;border-bottom:2px solid #222222;white-space:nowrap;}.frac .d{display:block;padding:0 6px;white-space:nowrap;}.eq{text-align:center;font-size:26px;color:#222222;margin:8px 0;}</style><p class=\"eq\" style=\"font-size:26px;\"><span class=\"frac\"><span class=\"n\">1</span><span class=\"d\">2</span></span> + <span class=\"frac\"><span class=\"n\">1</span><span class=\"d\">2</span></span> = <span class=\"frac\"><span class=\"n\">1 + 1</span><span class=\"d\">2</span></span> = <span class=\"frac\"><span class=\"n\">2</span><span class=\"d\">2</span></span></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "One half plus one half equals two over two.",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "d8ad1e85-baf6-43bc-89c1-e7d989670166",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "d8ad1e85-baf6-43bc-89c1-e7d989670166",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "thinking",
         "source_menu": [],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Vamos Pensar!\n\nPodemos também representar os dedos das duas mãos usando frações?",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "8b188a2a-6e5b-4883-8bb7-69fce4a2f40b",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": "yes",
         "score": 2,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "8b188a2a-6e5b-4883-8bb7-69fce4a2f40b",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "inlove",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "9b0e87f9-e372-49d4-979e-4ba9742f70e1",
               "text": "Texto Original",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=9b0e87f9-e372-49d4-979e-4ba9742f70e1",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            },
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "b16d461d-eb7a-484b-a78b-b12336edf3c0",
               "text": "Weisstein, Eric W.",
               "page": "https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Multiple.html",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            },
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "857f1df2-38ce-4da0-9444-686e16ac2314",
               "text": "Entendendo a Tabuada de Multiplicação (4 e 5)",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=857f1df2-38ce-4da0-9444-686e16ac2314",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2025",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Os Lados do Corpo\n\nO nosso corpo também pode ser entendido, inicialmente, como tendo dois lados (por enquanto, vamos ignorar a terceira dimensão — a profundidade). Se quisermos representar os dedos por lado, poderíamos escrever os dedos como:",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<style>.frac{display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;text-align:center;margin:0 6px;white-space:nowrap;}.frac .n{display:block;padding:0 6px;border-bottom:2px solid #222222;white-space:nowrap;}.frac .d{display:block;padding:0 6px;white-space:nowrap;}.eq{text-align:center;font-size:26px;color:#222222;margin:8px 0;}</style><p class=\"eq\" style=\"font-size:26px;\"><span class=\"frac\"><span class=\"n\">5</span><span class=\"d\">2</span></span> + <span class=\"frac\"><span class=\"n\">5</span><span class=\"d\">2</span></span> = <span class=\"frac\"><span class=\"n\">5 + 5</span><span class=\"d\">2</span></span> = <span class=\"frac\"><span class=\"n\">10</span><span class=\"d\">2</span></span> = 5</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "Five over two plus five over two equals ten over two equals five.",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "b33eff32-c797-4c27-a9e4-755a7a77a0a0",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
